{"lines":[{"h":0.013081395234588733,"t":"F","x":0.08082706764689282,"w":0.015037593841552732,"y":0.43459302320392657,"c":1},{"t":"G","y":0.59738372094848124,"w":0.016917292277018228,"c":1,"h":0.014534883321060788,"x":0.080827068029723961},{"c":1,"t":"H","w":0.016917292277018228,"x":0.078947368820764086,"y":0.77906976738997313,"h":0.013081395234588733},{"w":0.076203893025716174,"y":0.078906426726662815,"t":"Reading","h":0.016671248888554868,"c":1,"x":0.78716258123098759},{"h":0.017461514519017785,"t":"that any attempts to use the existing data were likely to be fundamentally flawed.","y":0.12645348863962558,"c":1,"x":0.12406016829157844,"w":0.71428568522135416},{"w":0.68631266276041658,"t":"Over the course of several seasons of fieldwork they carried out new surveys,","h":0.019844610308802579,"c":1,"x":0.12584270157061145,"y":0.14298809435454363},{"h":0.017505503284186652,"c":1,"w":0.6541353352864584,"x":0.124060151742356,"t":"finding an astonishing 198 settlement sites that were previously unknown.","y":0.16279069753708009},{"c":1,"t":"Now, research published by Dr Yama Dixit and Professor David Hodell, both","x":0.12406013957322244,"h":0.017707662588538287,"y":0.19896973569244059,"w":0.67105265299479167},{"w":0.71052632649739589,"h":0.018895348808647294,"c":1,"y":0.2165697674503807,"x":0.12406014489131678,"t":"from Cambridge's Department of Earth Sciences, has provided the first definitive"},{"w":0.68248743693033853,"t":"evidence for climate change affecting the plains of north-western India, where","x":0.12586320512318916,"h":0.019934331227024371,"y":0.23322531844773109,"c":1},{"w":0.69736841837565111,"t":"hundreds of Harappan sites are known to have been situated. The researchers","c":1,"y":0.25434642624091186,"h":0.016097875080489321,"x":0.12406015161646271},{"t":"gathered shells of Melanoides tuberculata snails from the sediments of an ancient","c":1,"x":0.12400453527867465,"y":0.27027092392557872,"w":0.72378519694010424,"h":0.017547050446598211},{"t":"lake and used geochemical analysis as a means of tracing the climate history of","c":1,"h":0.017707662588538287,"y":0.28911783665357571,"w":0.71052632649739578,"x":0.12218044583830533},{"y":0.30652211402729335,"c":1,"w":0.72191726684570323,"x":0.12399870983211997,"h":0.020335463347622262,"t":"the region. 'As today, the major source of water into the lake is likely to have been"},{"w":0.73120300292968765,"h":0.018895348808647294,"t":"the summer monsoon,' says Dixit. 'But we have observed that there was an abrupt","x":0.12218045314966379,"y":0.32412790697553717,"c":1},{"x":0.12406015277849784,"w":0.68796991984049483,"h":0.017441860722175351,"c":1,"y":0.3444767440547396,"t":"change about 4,100 years ago, when the amount of evaporation from the lake"},{"t":"exceeded the rainfall - indicative of a drought.' Hodell adds: 'We estimate that the","w":0.71992482503255206,"x":0.12406014383149871,"y":0.36188023155959026,"h":0.017480233678185297,"c":1},{"w":0.71428573608398438,"c":1,"h":0.015988372635703296,"t":"weakening of the Indian summer monsoon climate lasted about 200 years before","y":0.38081395321441103,"x":0.12406013939668639},{"h":0.022012510379513683,"t":"recovering to the previous conditions, which we still see today.'","c":1,"x":0.12208629799214857,"w":0.55854151407877617,"y":0.39673913324876331},{"h":0.020303179660460469,"t":"It has long been thought that other great Bronze Age civilisations also declined at","y":0.43210251830558,"x":0.12397453532375702,"c":1,"w":0.71634195963541669},{"x":0.12406014933252778,"w":0.71616541544596357,"h":0.017535452833501219,"t":"a similar time, with a global-scale climate event being seen as the cause. While it","y":0.45348837196203018,"c":1},{"t":"is possible that these local-scale processes were linked, the real archaeological","h":0.018995492594977459,"x":0.12030075197379432,"c":1,"y":0.46941403750153743,"w":0.70676691691080729},{"t":"interest lies in understanding the impact of these larger-scale events on different","y":0.48837209329078834,"w":0.71428568522135416,"h":0.017441859494004786,"x":0.12030076678781911,"c":1},{"y":0.50726744172850224,"w":0.73496241251627614,"t":"environments and different populations. 'Considering the vast area of the Harappan","h":0.01752328596342323,"x":0.12406014705242674,"c":1},{"h":0.020423710461362821,"w":0.73684209187825522,"c":1,"x":0.12406015759470695,"y":0.52318094034084794,"t":"Civilisation with its variable weather systems,' explains Singh, 'it is essential that we"},{"x":0.12400842409385632,"h":0.018101681146173387,"t":"obtain more climate data from areas close to the two great cities at Mohenjodaro","w":0.71062245686848957,"c":1,"y":0.54349685187574104},{"x":0.12406016565914285,"h":0.020418095880374465,"w":0.41541351318359371,"t":"and Harappa and also from the Indian Punjab.'","y":0.55813953478645206,"c":1},{"h":0.017707662588538287,"c":1,"t":"Petrie and Singh's team is now examining archaeological records and trying to","y":0.59723116545433963,"w":0.69360900878906251,"x":0.12218045793678679},{"x":0.12399404717611845,"w":0.69565500895182297,"h":0.020967363159808516,"c":1,"y":0.61277759121598574,"t":"understand details of how people led their lives in the region five millennia ago."},{"x":0.12406015157171225,"y":0.63361236290741396,"h":0.017707662588538287,"t":"They are analysing grains cultivated at the time, and trying to work out whether","w":0.697368418375651,"c":1},{"t":"they were grown under extreme conditions of water stress, and whether they","x":0.12218044472082966,"y":0.65260785553202927,"w":0.67669174194335935,"h":0.01745028412887073,"c":1},{"t":"were adjusting the combinations of crops they were growing for different weather","x":0.12218044014092745,"y":0.66999356097587048,"h":0.017506439150032138,"c":1,"w":0.71428573608398438},{"t":"systems. They are also looking at whether the types of pottery used, and other","w":0.69360900878906251,"y":0.68895348823897351,"h":0.01744186072217524,"x":0.12406015720172917,"c":1},{"t":"aspects of their material culture, were distinctive to specific regions or were more","x":0.12218044067511319,"y":0.70637475840465347,"w":0.71428573608398449,"h":0.017462450998948609,"c":1},{"w":0.66917292277018225,"h":0.015988372635703185,"t":"similar across larger areas. This gives us insight into the types of interactive","c":1,"x":0.12218045581559399,"y":0.7252906974006339},{"x":0.12209979340818677,"h":0.021288581302836951,"t":"networks that the population was involved in, and whether those changed.","w":0.65620803833007812,"y":0.7414609640000358,"c":1},{"x":0.1240601384226926,"c":1,"t":"Petrie believes that archaeologists are in a unique position to investigate how","h":0.015988372635703185,"w":0.68045115152994795,"y":0.77906976716821685},{"x":0.12218044802949748,"w":0.71052632649739589,"y":0.7965116276040286,"h":0.01744186072217524,"c":1,"t":"past societies responded to environmental and climatic change. 'By investigating"},{"y":0.81540697646935523,"c":1,"x":0.12218045562704816,"t":"responses to environmental pressures and threats, we can learn from the past to","w":0.71240600585937497,"h":0.015988372635703185},{"c":1,"t":"engage with the public, and the relevant governmental and administrative bodies,","x":0.12400858133842026,"w":0.71814819335937496,"h":0.018931243316787971,"y":0.83283687974981435},{"h":0.015988372635703185,"t":"to be more proactive in issues such as the management and administration of","x":0.1203007642182799,"y":0.851744185772907,"w":0.68984959920247402,"c":1},{"y":0.86918604637962393,"c":1,"t":"water supply, the balance of urban and rural development, and the importance of","w":0.71428573608398438,"h":0.017484913007413283,"x":0.12218044018300257},{"t":"preserving cultural heritage in the future.'","c":1,"x":0.12192771815411613,"h":0.023043681020055051,"w":0.36711985270182296,"y":0.88359487157223149},{"t":"69","c":1,"y":0.968023255816572,"w":0.024436090787251841,"x":0.83458646579841678,"h":0.013081395234588733}],"w":2400,"h":3106}